# Claude Drive — built on the user's loop (open fifths A2/E3 then F2/C3;
# D then C on top of the A, A then D on top of the F). The Kokoro choir
# bounce of that loop is the bed. Counted at 102 bpm: each chord is two
# bars, the choir file (two loops) is 32 beats, and the drums get a
# half-time feel. On top: patches/claude-drive.patch (three saws and sub,
# ladder + tape drive pinned, gentle filter), a syncopated bass, and a
# lead that answers the choir instead of doubling it — it leaves bar 1
# to the sung note, enters on a pickup, and keeps one rhythmic cell
# (two sixteenths into a long note) while the pitches develop. White
# keys only; the leans are the diatonic half-steps B->C and E->F.
#
# One loop = 16 beats = | Am | Am | F | F |

bpm 102
gate 0.9
tail 5

section INTRO 0..16
section A 16..48
section B 48..112
section C 112..144
section D 144..208

# every drive knob to maximum on the buses the patch can't reach; the kit
# dusted so it sits under the sung bed (bus lowpass, no kick click, dull hats)
automate dr_drive
1
automate bd_drive
1
automate tape_drive
1
automate tape_age
0.3
automate dr_tone
0.4
automate bd_attack
0.1
automate hh_metal
0.15

# ---- the bed: the sung loop, two cycles per file, locked to 32 beats ----
track bed sample=renders/kokoro-choir-am-f.wav root=C4 fixed loop beats=32 gain=0.9 attack=0.02 release=2
C4:208

# ---- bass: syncopated, rests and octave pops, every loop placed by hand ----
# each line is one loop: | Am | Am | F | F |
track bass patch=claude-drive vel=0.8 len=0.5 gain=1.25 duck=0.3
>A
A1:0.75 A1:0.75@0.6 A1:0.5 R:1 A2:0.5@0.7 R:0.5 | A1:0.75 A1:0.75@0.6 R:0.5 A1:0.5 G1:0.5@0.7 R:1 | F1:0.75 F1:0.75@0.6 F1:0.5 R:1 F2:0.5@0.7 R:0.5 | F1:0.75 F1:0.75@0.6 R:0.5 F1:0.5 E1:0.5@0.7 G1:0.5@0.6 R:0.5
A1:0.75 A1:0.75@0.6 A1:0.5 R:0.5 E2:0.5@0.6 A2:0.5@0.7 R:0.5 | A1:0.75 A1:0.75@0.6 R:0.5 A1:0.5 G1:0.75@0.7 R:0.75 | F1:0.75 F1:0.75@0.6 F1:0.5 R:0.5 C2:0.5@0.6 F2:0.5@0.7 R:0.5 | F1:0.75 F1:0.75@0.6 R:0.5 F1:0.5 E1:0.75@0.7 R:0.75
>B
A1:0.75 A1:0.75@0.65 A1:0.5@0.9 R:1 A2:0.5@0.75 R:0.5 | A1:0.75 A1:0.75@0.65 R:0.5 A1:0.5 G1:0.5@0.75 A1:0.5@0.6 R:0.5 | F1:0.75 F1:0.75@0.65 F1:0.5@0.9 R:1 F2:0.5@0.75 R:0.5 | F1:0.75 F1:0.75@0.65 R:0.5 F1:0.5 E1:0.5@0.75 G1:0.5@0.65 R:0.5
A1:0.75 A1:0.75@0.65 A1:0.5@0.9 R:0.5 E2:0.5@0.6 A2:0.5@0.75 R:0.5 | A1:0.75 A1:0.75@0.65 R:0.5 A1:0.5 G1:0.75@0.75 R:0.75 | F1:0.75 F1:0.75@0.65 F1:0.5@0.9 R:0.5 C2:0.5@0.6 F2:0.5@0.75 R:0.5 | F1:0.75 F1:0.75@0.65 R:0.5 F1:0.5 E1:0.75@0.75 R:0.75
A1:0.75 A1:0.75@0.65 A1:0.5@0.9 R:1 A2:0.5@0.75 R:0.5 | A1:0.75 A1:0.75@0.65 R:0.5 A1:0.5 B1:0.5@0.7 C2:0.5@0.7 R:0.5 | F1:0.75 F1:0.75@0.65 F1:0.5@0.9 R:1 F2:0.5@0.75 R:0.5 | F1:0.75 F1:0.75@0.65 R:0.5 F1:0.5 G1:0.5@0.7 E1:0.5@0.7 R:0.5
A1:0.75 A1:0.75@0.65 A1:0.5@0.9 R:0.5 E2:0.5@0.6 A2:0.5@0.75 R:0.5 | A1:0.75 A1:0.75@0.65 R:0.5 A1:0.5 G1:0.5@0.75 A1:0.25@0.6 A1:0.25@0.6 R:0.5 | F1:0.75 F1:0.75@0.65 F1:0.5@0.9 R:0.5 C2:0.5@0.6 F2:0.5@0.75 R:0.5 | F1:0.75 F1:0.75@0.65 R:0.5 F1:0.5 E1:0.5@0.75 E1:0.25@0.6 E1:0.25@0.6 R:0.5
>C
A1:3 R:1 | A1:2 E2:1.5@0.6 G1:0.5@0.6 | F1:3 R:1 | F1:2 C2:1.5@0.6 E1:0.5@0.6
A1:3 R:1 | A1:2 E2:1@0.6 G1:1@0.6 | F1:3 R:1 | F1:1.5 R:0.5 C2:1@0.6 E1:0.5@0.7 G1:0.5@0.7
